-- title:
--   Borel-invariant elements form the Γ₀(qM') function field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ such that some ring homomorphism $\iota_0:L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) at level $q^2M'$ with group [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), i.e. the $L$-subfield of Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-field generated by the ratios $\,\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions (width $1$) of weight-$k$ modular forms on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where $H$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $\tau$ assign to each $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$, and assume that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the automorphism $\tau\gamma$ satisfies `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$ at the data $(L,q,\zeta,q,q^2M',H)$: for all $k$, all weight-$k$ forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_{\mathbb{Q}}\,p_g\ne 0$, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_{\mathbb{Q}}p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}_{\mathbb{Q}}p_g$, and every $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta=e^{2\pi i/q}$, one has $\iota_*\big(\tau\gamma(x)\big)\cdot \mathrm{qExp}_1\big(g\mid_k \gamma^{-1,\sharp}\big)=\mathrm{qExp}_1\big(f\mid_k\gamma^{-1,\sharp}\big)$, where $\delta^{\sharp}=\mathrm{diag}(q,1)^{-1}\delta\,\mathrm{diag}(q,1)=\begin{pmatrix}a&b/q\\qc&d\end{pmatrix}$. Then for $w\in K$: $\tau\gamma(w)=w$ for all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ whose upper-right entry is divisible by $q$ if and only if the Laurent series underlying $w$ lies in the $L$-base change of the $\mathbb{Q}$-function field generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_0(qM')$.
--
--   This identifies the fixed field of the Borel-type subgroup $\{\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M'): q\mid b\}$, acting through the level automorphisms, as the $L$-base change of the modular function field of level $\Gamma_0(qM')$, in Shimura's description of the fields generated by $q$-expansion ratios of modular forms. It is used in the full-level analysis of the modular curve $X_H(q^2M')$, in the statements about comparison with the $\Gamma_0(qM')$ level, ramification indices and the cyclic inertia action.
